why does the crab feeder's freaky mask  look so freaking familiar you're not  imagining it here's the surprising  connection the villain's headgear has to  game of thrones spoilers ahead  hbo's highly anticipated prequel series  house of the dragon is pulling in  massive numbers for the network proving  that viewers are happy to return to the  fantasy world of westeros and in droves  one intriguing element of the show thus  far is its swift introduction and then  justice swift killing off of the  villainous crab feeder aka cragus drajar  the crab feeder is backed by powerful  entities within the free cities who wish  to see westeros weakened  the masked greyscale afflicted baddies  served as the first major outside threat  to the targaryen protagonists however  there's also something about him that  surprisingly connects crab feeder  directly to game of thrones in an  interview with entertainment weekly crab  feeder actor daniel scott smith talked  extensively about his time as the  character on house of the dragon among  the more interesting tidbits was scott  smith confirming a cool detail about his  character's mask and its ties to a  well-known game of thrones cult the sons  of the harpy he told the outlet that he  discussed the mask with the director of  episodes 2 and 3 saying we spoke about  the idea of him being the first person  to wear this mask and it becoming iconic  and therefore it's built from that for  game of thrones why is he wearing the  mask how does he feel about that it's a  power statement so he's quite happy  wearing it well this is a fascinating  connection for house of the dragon to  make to its parent show it obviously  raises more questions than it answers  what inspired the sons of the harpy to  start wearing masks modeled after the  one that crab feeder wore is he  something of a legendary figure for them  or does it have some deeper perhaps  religious connotations and perhaps most  importantly of all will the showrunners  dive into this topic further or will it  be saved for some other far-off spin-off  series regardless it's still a big  connection between the shows that die  hard fans will no doubt appreciate damon  targaryen kills crab feeder off-screen  in episode 3 and the first serious  outside antagonist the family faces in  house of the dragon is gone in the blink  of an eye scott smith told ew that he  never even met matt smith on the set and  that it was bizarre to see his own  prosthetic corpse on tv it's a strange  experience i don't think many people  would experience that normally but it  was quite surreal it was cool though the  crab feeder never speaks but the  reappearance of the gold mask and house  of the dragon helps visually signify  that this person is an enemy of the  targaryens just as the sons of the harpy  were in game of thrones fans of the  original series will remember the  resistance group as one of daenerys  targaryen's foes in seasons 5 and 6. the  group forms to combat daenerys and her  new rule of marine the gold mask is a  representation of the harpy a gold  figure with the head and torso of a  woman and the wings tail and legs of a  bird this was a symbol of the slave  masters in slaver's bay so why crab  feeder would be wearing the same mask as  a bit of a question mark his armies are  from the free cities so perhaps this  gold mask is just a way for house of the  dragon to identify a foe of house  targaryen or perhaps it was just  something thrown in for game of thrones  stands daniel scott smith admitted that  was a factor in his ew interview saying  it was definitely a nod to that for i  guess the fans because it's something  familiar for them
 

